  "_note": "Videos on the site, one entry per clip; {lang} in a path becomes cs or en. A set of clips goes on the site with `npm run media:use -- <folder> --date YYYY-MM-DD` (one clip: edit its row, then `npm run media:use -- <folder> --keep-rest`), which checks it and writes clip_date (the recording date shown in the captions, {clip.date}; null = the sentence is left out), version (?v= on the addresses, because /video/* is cached as immutable and clips keep their names) and clips.tour.chapters (from tour.chapters.json). clips.ats.clip_date is V6's own date ({clip.ats_date}): V6 is not retaken with the rest, so media:use leaves it alone. sources: in the order the browser tries them, the first that fits wins; { src, type, media?, width?, height?, budget_mb? }, media for a version by pixel density such as \"(min-resolution: 1.5dppx) and (min-width: 768px)\", with its own size and budget; the last one must be an MP4 for every screen, any other format goes by taking out its rows. cues: the line under the video, { at, at_mobile?, key }, seconds and a key of the text map. Display widths: tokens.css --video-*. A clip's own clip_date is the day that clip was recorded (hero: {clip.hero_date}, its phone cut {clip.hero_phone_date}). by_lang.<lang> replaces what it names for one language, the older cut of a language still waiting; taking it out is the change. waits: this cut is not the final one, what replaces it; check:release says so until it is gone. at_mobile null: a line the phone cut does not have. All times of the text under a clip are in its cues here, nowhere else.",
